Turnip (Vulkan) on Darwin over the BlueGPU user client: the msm KMD backend through the
bluedrm libdrm stand-in. Darwin enumeration (no /dev/dri: drmOpenWithType("msm")), BO maps
via bluedrm_map/unmap (no placed maps), no SET_IOVA (one shared VA space, kernel-chosen
IOVAs), bluedrm.c compiled into Turnip, bluedrm-backed DRM syncobjs for vk_drm_syncobj (HAVE_BLUEDRM_SYNCOBJ), no DRM WSI,
condvar on CLOCK_REALTIME, CTR_EL0 constant (EL0 read traps on XNU) and
-undefined dynamic_lookup for the weak entrypoint tables. The last three follow UniXNU
patches/mesa/turnip-darwin-kmd.patch (MIT).

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -816,7 +816,7 @@
